ody, regarded as a loner.\n\nWe need to make a short argumentative contribution, state or imply current hiring recommendation, refer to existing discussion, use explicit facts, explain why evidence supports or weakens candidate's case, consistent with our vote.\n\nWe need to decide our vote. We have previously voted for B in round 2, then after Agent 1's argument we might reconsider. The panel currently has Agent 1 recommending C, Agent 2 also recommending C, Agent 3 currently voted B earlier but now we can change. We need to decide based on evidence. The lack of crew cooperation evidence for B is a serious gap. C has positive crew atmosphere despite communication issues. So likely we will shift to C. So we will vote Candidate C.\n\nWe need to reference Agent 1's point about lack of data on A and D, and that B lacks positive crew cooperation. We can argue that given the critical importance of crew cooperation, and that C demonstrates positive crew atmosphere, C remains best. Also we can note that C's communication difficulty is a concern but can be mitigated, whereas B's lack of cooperation evidence is a bigger risk. So we will agree with Agent 1 and reaffirm C.\n\nThus public message: \"I agree with Agent 1; the lack of any positive crew cooperation evidence for B, combined with C's proven positive crew atmosphere, outweighs C's communication concerns. Therefore I also recommend Candidate C.\"\n\nMake sure to include explicit facts: C creates positive crew atmosphere, 100% reliability, rapid correct decisions, calm in crisis; B makes nasty remarks, pretentious, wrong tone, no positive cooperation evidence. Also note that A and D have no data on key criteria, so cannot be considered.\n\nVote: Candidate C.\n\nNow produce output."}
